export const initialState={powerRole:'bridge',systemFocus:'all'};
const scene=(id,label,title,reference,explanation,sources,extra={})=>({id,label,title,reference,objective:'integration',pedagogical_role:'case-study',explanation:[explanation],sources,...extra});
const S=finaleSources;
export const scenes=[
 scene('abilene-factory','Abilene','Putting an AI Factory Together','d15-upgrade-and-evidence','Return to the original Oracle/OpenAI campus. The closing chapter follows one real facility through workload requirements, supply, heat rejection, delivery and finance. The adjacent Microsoft project is a separate development. The photograph is Oracle’s July 15, 2026 aerial; it does not establish how many depicted halls were operating.',[S.campus],{pedagogical_role:'opening'}),
 scene('abilene-workload','Start with the workload','The GB200 cluster shapes the building around it.','d02-workload-brief','OpenAI reported the first GB200 racks arriving in June 2025 and early training and inference by July. Connect this real workload to three interfaces: rack power, liquid and residual-air heat capture, and the fabric that connects racks. These are the same interfaces taught earlier, now requirements on a real campus. Do not infer tokens per second, a particular model, GPU inventory or utilization from the campus rating.',[S.workloads,S.live]),
 scene('abilene-power','Bridge power becomes backup','Abilene’s gas plant has a role before and after grid expansion.','d03-power-and-procurement','Crusoe’s 2025 Impact Report describes 350 MW of on-site gas generation as temporary bridge power and long-term backup. Toggle the plant’s role while keeping the same equipment. Bridge generation can advance delivery, but requires fuel infrastructure, emissions controls and operation; the equipment then retains a continuity role. This conceptual supply diagram does not specify installed switchgear, source proportions or transfer timing. The gas rating does not establish backup for the full planned campus.',[S.impact],{controls:[{key:'powerRole',label:'Gas plant role',options:[['bridge','Bridge power'],['backup','Long-term backup']]}]}),
 scene('abilene-heat','Water shapes the cooling','Abilene chose air-cooled chillers to conserve water.','d11-heat-rejection','Crusoe describes a recirculating facility-water loop with air-cooled chillers, accepting higher lifecycle and maintenance costs for water conservation. Follow heat across the rack-side and facility-side interfaces to the refrigerant condenser and outdoor air. The diagram summarizes those functions without claiming an as-built pipe arrangement or a particular residual-air device. A closed facility loop still needs initial fill and maintenance water.',[S.design]),
 scene('abilene-hot-day','Follow the operating cost','Hotter air can raise the power bill for the same IT load.','d11-weather-and-operating-envelope','Apply the air-cooled chiller mechanism to the documented design. With the same IT duty and coolant target, hotter condenser air generally requires higher refrigerant condensing temperature and compressor work; outdoor heat rejection includes that extra work. Show the same installed racks in both conditions. This is a qualitative operating comparison, not measured Abilene performance. At equipment limits, the permitted IT load may need to fall; no site-specific threshold or derating curve is published here.',[S.chiller]),
 scene('abilene-parallel-build','Build in parallel','Abilene manufactured electrical equipment while the site took shape.','d13-delivery-dependencies','Crusoe reports in-house switchgear manufacture and prefabricated electrical skids for Abilene. The two parallel lanes represent factory work and site work converging at installation and testing, without fabricated lead times. Preserve the valuable lesson from the former retrofit case: the package must meet electrical interfaces and remain accessible for installation and maintenance. Factory completion alone does not establish an operating hall.',[S.impact]),
 scene('abilene-capital','Finance the physical campus','Long-term demand supports investment in the buildings.','d15-cost-per-service','The initial project was fully leased long-term to an unnamed hyperscaler in the October 2024 financing announcement. In May 2025 Crusoe, Blue Owl and Primary Digital announced the second phase of a $15 billion joint venture for the campus. Treat the venture as facility funding: it is not a disclosed GPU purchase bill, cloud revenue or profit. The diagram connects the facility investment to the customer’s capacity commitment without inventing loan terms or the Oracle/OpenAI billing rate.',[S.capital,S.lease]),
 scene('abilene-live-expansion','Grow around live workloads','Abilene ran its first workloads while the campus kept growing.','d13-commissioning-complete-paths','The first two buildings were energized within a year of the June 2024 construction start; the project continued toward eight buildings and an integrated network fabric. The drawing preserves the distinction between a working phase and construction. Use it to discuss the interfaces of the next phase: electrical connection, heat rejection and network change. Keeping them isolated until ready is the engineering implication, not a claim about a published Abilene commissioning procedure or topology. This replaces the old acceptance-flag quiz and invented six-/seven-/twelve-day schedule.',[S.live,S.workloads]),
 scene('watts-to-work','From Watts to Tokens','From Watts to Tokens','d15-upgrade-and-evidence','Close on the complete system. Follow source power into distribution, then split it between IT and cooling equipment; follow information through the cluster into OpenAI workloads; follow rack heat and cooling electricity to the outdoor condenser. Contracts and capital enabled the physical construction, while the model and workload determine actual output. Highlight the three paths rather than turn the campus rating into an invented token rate. The map is functional: it makes no claim about exact equipment counts, detailed redundancy or as-built routing.',[S.design,S.live],{pedagogical_role:'synthesis',controls:[{key:'systemFocus',label:'Trace the campus',options:[['all','Whole system'],['power','Power'],['information','Information'],['heat','Heat']]}]})
];
